            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0249" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 167.</note>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">No. 146.]</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1870</date>. (Received October
                    20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have this moment received, a little in
                    advance of the press, a lithographic copy of Count Bismarck’s account of his
                    interview with Jules Favre. Having no time to make a translation or abstract of
                    it before the closing of the mail, I send you the document as I received it from
                    the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For a translation of this inclosure see Baron Gerolt’s note to Mr. Fish of
                        October 17, 1870, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
